# Shell scripts must keep LF endings and stay executable.
#
# Both matter only off-Windows, which is exactly why they are easy to break from
# a Windows checkout and impossible to notice there:
#   * CRLF endings make the `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang fail on macOS/Linux
#     with a confusing "bad interpreter: ... ^M" error.
#   * the executable bit is not tracked by the Windows filesystem
#     (core.filemode=false), so a script can be committed non-executable and
#     then fail with "permission denied" for anyone who clones on macOS/Linux.
#     Fix that with: git update-index --chmod=+x <path>
*.sh text eol=lf
